<!-- Why Cooperative AI Section -->
<section class="py-20 bg-yellow-50">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 text-center mb-12">
      Why Cooperative AI
    </h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-6 text-gray-700">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        The development of advanced AI will give rise to autonomous multi-agent systems that could pose novel risks. To ensure that complex AI systems are developed in a safe and equitable manner for the flourishing of all humans, risks related to alignment and multi-agent systems must be mitigated.
      </p>
      
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        The field of AI safety aims to resolve alignment and safety issues in AI systems for both short and long term existential risk. Cooperative AI focuses on the interactions that arise in complex systems. Here is a list of resources to learn more about cooperative AI.
      </p>
      
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Through the Cooperative AI South Africa fellowship, we are supporting global talent in advancing research in this crucial phase of AI development. Our partners in South Africa and abroad aim to facilitate collaboration across continents to solve safety and alignment problems, enabling researchers to build ongoing relationships that lead to impactful careers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Why South Africa Section -->
<section class="py-20 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 text-center mb-12">
      Why South Africa
    </h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-6 text-gray-700">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        This program aims to support the burgeoning AI Safety ecosystem in South Africa, including the establishment of the African AI Safety Hub at the University of Cape Town. By the end of this fellowship, we hope to identify 2-3 fellows to be recommended for full-time research positions at this new institution.
      </p>
      
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        For philosophical reasons, Africa has a connection to the collectivist epistemics that underlie Cooperative AI through the widely held value system of "Ubuntu", which emphasises the interconnectedness of individuals with their surrounding societal and physical world. By following a community-oriented model, we can develop a high-impact local network of AI Safety researchers to help shape the global AI trajectory.
      </p>
      
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        CAIF's research agenda resonates deeply with these values. Through this collaboration, we can support emerging talent in Africa, engage diverse voices in AI Safety, create an international CAI hub, and provide CAIF with the densest ML talent pool on the continent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
